grainworks.tech
a manifesto

the machine is already running.

data centers hum whether you're logged on or not. models have been trained on data stolen from all of humanity. compute is being burned on slop. this isn't whether we use ai but what for.

we acknowledge the contradiction. ai's environmental cost is real. its corporate capture is entrenched. the technology was not built to set us free. and so, the cat is out of the bag. retreating to a private bunker is not an option for us. 

so what do we actually do with it?

do we replace the creative process? the struggles that humans endure in pursuit of growth? no, we need tools that claw back time, attention, and agency from tech run amok. not optimization for its own sake.

grainworks is a research lab for the humane use of ai tools. we dream, build, and test things that reduce the friction of being alive under capitalism. wood, steel, electrons, and lines of code are all the same to us.

why can't ai do your laundry? what does your ai agent really know about you?

we want to know.

modern technology fights for human attention. we're interested in tools that don't.

as we sand and treat wood, so we work with the grain of humanity.

things that help people organize, understand, repair, connect, and grow... without selling their data or dignity.

this is not a professional blog... this is not thought leadership. this is a workshop. we publish what we build, what we learn, and what breaks. if it's useful to someone else, that's the point.

the machines are running. let's make it worth it.

